    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="1318" n="1222" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1222"/>

                <head>No. 813.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Russell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-11-25"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 25,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 29.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 31, of the 6th instant,
                    has been received. It relates to the benevolent conduct of Messrs. H. L. Boulton
                    &amp; Co., toward immigrants from this country in distress in Venezuela. The
                    course of those gentlemen in this instance does them honor, and you will offer
                    them the thanks of this Government therefor.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
